# text_id = 1719
# text = It was a long time ago that General Smuts first preached the idea of an African Council by which nations would get together , regardless of their frontiers and without the slightest detriment to their sovereignty , to fight those things which do not recognise frontiers — disease and famine , the tsetse fly , the rinderpest and other scourges .
