# text = I would say , however , to the Chancellor of the Exchequer that although we do not intend to - day to discuss general expenditure upon the war , the House of Commons will insist on keeping control over such expenditure and , from time to time , the Opposition parties will require ample opportunities for the discussion of that expenditure .
