# text_id = 1788
# text = It is perfectly true that Regulation 58AA and the National Arbitration Order both cover only strikes which take place in connection with a trade dispute , and it is suggested , as I understand it , on behalf of the Government that if a strike is not in relation to a trade dispute , it is probably perfectly legal .
