# text_id = 1800
# text = I think all English people — if I may say so , as a Celt — rather tend to regard criminal justice as something rather like fox - hunting — an elaborate ritual to be followed with highly technical rules in which , whatever is done , the fox must not be shot but may be torn to pieces by hounds .
