# text = He was anxious for the local authorities to get on with their housing programmes , and he sent a directive to the local authorities in the blitzed areas suggesting that they should relinquish the work of war damage repairs and leave the repairs to the owners of the properties concerned in consultation with the office of the Commission and private builders , and concentrate all their attention on building houses .
