# text_id = 1877
# text = Sir R. Glyn asked the Minister of Food whether , in order to reduce congestion and consequent cruelty to animals sent for slaughter , he will now consider the advantage of allowing 50 per cent . of the licensed slaughterhouses in each local authority area to be licensed that were licensed in 1938 , as such action will improve the quality of the meat and reduce the demands on transport .
