# text = Lieut .-Commander Joynson - Hicks asked the Secretary of State for War what steps are being taken to remove the palisades , barbed wire and other military defences from the shore in those areas to which access has recently been regranted to the population ; whether the local authorities concerned have been informed of the arrangements ; and if the cost of restoration is to the account of his department .
