# text_id = 1934
# text = There was no corresponding legislation for England , and I imagine that what was in the mind of my predecessor — because it was in his time — and the Government of the day was that it was most important in England , where there had been an even greater reduction of housing accommodation than in Scotland , not to dry up in any way the supply of furnished lettings .
