# text_id = 1937
# text = General Sir George Jeffreys asked the Assistant Postmaster - General whether he is aware that the present form in which telephone accounts are issued to subscribers is drawn up in such a manner that the accounts are difficult to comprehend and compare most unfavourably with accounts rendered by ordinary business firms ; and when he anticipates that it will be possible to issue these accounts in a more satisfactory form .
