# text_id = 1972
# text = Mr. McKinlay asked the Secretary of State for Scotland is he is aware that green crops planted in gardens of householders in Dumbartonshire , in response to the appeal to dig for victory , are being destroyed by ground vermin ; that the Scottish Office refuse to entertain any application for supplies of protective netting ; and will he now advise such householders of alternative means of safeguarding their crops .
