# text_id = 1973
# text = The noble and learned Viscount told us when this Bill was first introduced that he was " diametrically opposed " ( that , I think , was his phrase ) to what I may call the " Silverman clause , " and that he was confident that if it was carried it would mean a reduction in the deterrent effect of capital punishment , at any rate in some cases .
