# text_id = 1997
# text = In accepting any recommendation which may be made by such a committee , the Lord Chancellor assumes , and has to assume , that only persons who are so qualified are recommended to him by the advisory committee , and will not , of course , in any circumstances whatsoever , appoint any person in relation to whom there can be any question at all whether he is so suitable .
