# text = I would remind them , as they have already been reminded from this side , that it must have come as a great surprise to the Milk Marketing Board that in the prewar days the well - to - do section of the community consumed 5 ½ pints of milk per head per week , whereas in poorer sections of the community the quantity consumed was 1.1 pints per week .
