# text_id = 2059
# text = In the first place , as regards the clause in the Bill which abolishes the term " working - class dwelling , " it would be a relief to everybody if we were satisfied that never again in industrial towns should we see rows of back - to - back houses erected , or the approaches to London defiled by some of the architectural monstrosities that at present greet our view .
